    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0148" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p1/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/P–NSC files, lot 61 D 167, “North Africa”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Harry H.
                            Schwartz of the Policy Planning’ Staff to the Executive
                        Secretary, National Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d36-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-03-19">March 19, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>NSC Consideration of Africa</item>
                </list>
                <p>I submit herewith a list of African problems which have a bearing on United
                    States security interests in that Continent. This list is applicable to Africa
                    as a whole, but, as was brought out at the Planning Board meeting of March 3,
                    United States policy problems with respect to this extensive Continent should at
                    least be broken down into three main areas: North Africa (French North Africa
                    and Libya), the Union of South Africa, and the area between those two.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry H.
                            Schwartz</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">NSC Planning Board Assistant<lb/>Department
                            of State</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d36-a1.xml" xpointer="d36-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d36-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d36-f1-content">
                <p>Lay transmitted this memorandum and the
                    enclosed list to the NSC Planning Board on Mar.
                    19, 1954.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
